    "turn_idx": 287,
    "turn_text": "Well, let's review the entire situation. Why does Saudi Arabia have $600 to $700 billion into public investment fund? It's because we all use oil and we all drive cars. So we are responsible for filling up that public investment fund to tune the $600 to $700 billion. I mean, do we expect the Saudis to take that money and then just burn it? No, they're going to take that money and they're going to invest it. Now, in general, In general, it is good for foreigners to invest in America. That means our economy is doing well. It means that we have a stable political situation. And we encourage investment. That's what creates jobs. We need investment in this country. You know, both domestic and foreign investment. I would much rather have the Saudis modernize, respect human rights. and invest in America, then cozy up to China or Russia at this point in time. Start trading their oil in Chinese currency, as opposed to the petrol dial. So again, you can isolate and put the entire burden of the Saudis' human rights abuses on the PGA and expect them to show that full burden. But then that just denies the fact that We're the ones that use the oil to fill up the pith that give them the financial wherewithal to invest in all kinds of businesses in the u.s. not just p g i realize p g is a highly visible entity. But they're deep Saudi investments, all kinds of American businesses. Are we going to ask all those American businesses to divest, not accept those investments and watch the value of those stocks plummet? So again, we have a global integrated economy. And I think we need to understand how it's not just the PGA that is dealing with Saudis. We all are when we use oil.",
